# HVT Architecture

Hydra Viewport Toolbox builds on OpenUSD Hydra for viewport rendering. It **simplifies**
application integration (frame passes, managers, task pipelines) and **extends** OpenUSD with
additional features and helpers (WBOIT, outlines, geometry utilities, scene-index filters,
custom tasks, …).

## Layout

- Public API: `include/hvt/` — implementations in `source/` (same subdirectories)
- Engine (`include/hvt/engine/`): simplify viewport integration — frame passes, managers
- Tasks, scene index, geometry, pageable buffers: extend OpenUSD with HVT-specific capability
- Shaders: `include/hvt/resources/shaders/*.glslfx`
- Design docs: `docs/` — start with `docs/README.md`
- Unit tests: `test/tests/` — library validation; baselines in `test/data/baselines/`
- How-tos: `test/howTos/` — one usage demo per feature; prefer over inventing integration code

## Core model

```
FramePass
  ├── HdRetainedSceneIndex (shared)
  ├── TaskManager          → HdxTask pipeline (docs/taskmgr.md)
  ├── RenderBufferManager  → AOV Bprims (docs/renderbuffermgr.md)
  └── LightingManager      → light Sprims (docs/lightingmgr.md)
```

Tasks are stored as scene-index prims and executed in list order. Task commit functions run
before each frame to sync params from application state.

## Boundaries

- **Do not edit** `externals/vcpkg/` — dependency submodule only
- **Do not edit** generated `include/hvt/namespace.h` (created at configure time)
- Match existing patterns in neighboring files before introducing new abstractions
- Namespace: `HVT_NS`; export macro: `HVT_API` on public free functions only

## Agent entry points

| Task | Start here |
|------|------------|
